#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:110
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Already-adjudicated guidance: WHO SMART DAKs at L2 and FHIR Implementation Guides at L3. A recommendation adopted in a published DAK is evidence of a different kind from a primary study -- it is a prior decision, with its own provenance, and must be cited as that rather than laundered into primary evidence. NOT YET SKILL-BACKED. This step named `corpus-search`, which has never existed. It is not `corpus-grep`, whose job is the pre-declaration check that something really is an open gap — searching adjudicated L2/L3 content for evidence is a different task, so pointing the ref there would have been a plausible-looking wrong answer. Left uncovered until the skill is written."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:67
#. Diagram label
msgid "An edit is about to be drafted"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:157
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An unresolvable citation is not dropped and not silently kept. It becomes a tracked item, so the gap is visible in the work plan rather than surviving as a footnote nobody re-checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:151
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by checking the source against the observatory or registry API: is its authority confirmed? `no` opens a bean for the unverified citation; `yes` goes on to appraise and grade the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the appraisal: is the graded evidence enough to support a recommendation? `no` records the evidence gap; `yes` attaches the evidence to the recommendation."
msgstr ""

