#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Task_VerifyAuthority and its gateway sit here rather than with Lane_Agent because the decision is not this instance's call — it is a readout of what the external API returns, and the moment that answer is uncertain or absent, Lane_WorkPlan opens a bean rather than this lane inventing a verdict."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The appraisal in the role's own description happens elsewhere in this diagram: this lane only fans out in parallel across the three evidence classes and joins the candidates, while grading is Lane_Author's call and authority is Lane_Trusted's — so what it owns here is coverage, not judgement."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The author answers before any search starts. `yes`: the change states a recommendation or alters one, and the evidence is gathered as below. `no`: the change carries none -- a mathematics folio has none, and a figure redrawn from its own source as a computable graphic adds or changes none -- so there is nothing to frame as PICO. The `no` branch ends at its own event, which records that answer in the instance history; it does not pretend a search was run. The answer is the author's and the editor still rules on the change at Task_ReviewFindings in Process_Editing, so a wrong `no` is caught there."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:80
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The author reads what the document, DAK or IG ALREADY says on this question, before looking outward. A recommendation that contradicts a sibling recommendation in the same artefact is a defect no external evidence will reveal."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/evidence-retrieval.bpmn:196
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The PICO, the graded body of evidence, each verified citation and its resolved authority record are written onto the recommendation block, so a reader can retrace the whole chain from the sentence back to the source."
msgstr ""

